            <symbol type="1" id="44" code="203" name="Rocky pit or cave (without a distinct entrance)">
                <description>Rocky pits, holes, caves or mineshafts which may constitute a danger to the
competitor.

Location is the centre of gravity of the symbol, and the symbol shall be orientated
to north, except for caves with a distinct entrance, where the symbol
should point into the cave.

Rocky pits larger than 5 m in diameter should be exaggerated and represented
using cliff symbols (201, 202).

Minimum depth: 1 m.
Footprint: 10.5 m x 12 m.</description>
